{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And these are the kings, etc.</b> He intends by this to enumerate all that intermarried with Edom, or set up for her a king and the like, for all of it stands for destruction when Edom falls. As they said, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 83): Bozrah — because she set up a king for Edom — is destined to be struck together with them, as it is written (Isaiah 34:6): ״זֶבַח לַה׳ בְּבָצְרָה״ — end quote. So too the rest of the cities: even though they may pass from hand to hand before the Redeemer of the glory of Israel comes, the children of Israel will enter with a prior claim and expel them, and they will be burned, and no shadow of another will save them." "<b>Also</b> to take a sign for the future redemption, when the days grow long. And the proof: HaShem enumerated the kings of Edom, who preceded the kings of Israel; just as they [the kings of Edom] preceded, the kings of Israel preceded to their [future] kingship — after the cessation that followed the kings listed in the Torah. From this it follows that likewise Israel will reign for the same count as those who reigned in Edom (in exile — gloss). And even though the six thousand years stand (Sanhedrin 99a), may HaShem lengthen days of goodness, as they said, of blessed memory." "<b>Thus concludes the parashah of VaYishlaḥ</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 36, :notes {1 "The parenthetical (בגלות, הגהה) appears to be a printer's gloss; rendered literally as '(in exile — gloss).'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:18.654876353Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}